WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.134
(ethereal music)

00:00:03.134 --> 00:00:06.704
- When you're looking up at
a beautiful dark night sky,

00:00:06.704 --> 00:00:10.478
what goes through my
mind is the wonder of it.

00:00:10.478 --> 00:00:12.895
It's just so incredibly vast.

00:00:14.609 --> 00:00:16.134
I never lose interest in it,

00:00:16.134 --> 00:00:19.425
because it's just so beautiful.

00:00:19.425 --> 00:00:22.567
I wanted others to enjoy the night sky

00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:24.472
as much as they could.

00:00:24.472 --> 00:00:28.477
The best way to do that is to
build your own planetarium.

00:00:28.477 --> 00:00:31.043
(piano music)

00:00:31.043 --> 00:00:33.620
The Kovac planetarium is located

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:36.114
in the north woods of Wisconsin,

00:00:36.114 --> 00:00:38.531
in the little town of Monico.

00:00:39.434 --> 00:00:42.362
I began the project in 1997,

00:00:42.362 --> 00:00:46.362
and it was finally opened
to the public in 2007.

00:00:48.366 --> 00:00:50.173
I started from scratch,

00:00:50.173 --> 00:00:51.435
a lot of trial and error.

00:00:51.435 --> 00:00:53.102
I had no blueprints.

00:00:54.292 --> 00:00:55.709
There were many, many times

00:00:55.709 --> 00:00:59.181
where I had so many roadblocks come my way

00:00:59.181 --> 00:01:01.264
that I wanted to give up.

00:01:03.134 --> 00:01:05.175
I just had to convince
myself and my neighbors

00:01:05.175 --> 00:01:07.163
that I wasn't crazy.

00:01:07.163 --> 00:01:10.245
And of course, when I started
putting up this planetarium,

00:01:10.245 --> 00:01:15.059
that was when people really
started to wonder about me.

00:01:15.059 --> 00:01:16.883
So it's kind of neat.

00:01:16.883 --> 00:01:17.977
I built this thing,

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:20.677
and now I get to maintain it,

00:01:20.677 --> 00:01:23.126
keep it running for the shows.

00:01:23.126 --> 00:01:25.106
(twinkling music)

00:01:25.106 --> 00:01:28.584
This is the largest
mechanically-operated planetarium

00:01:28.584 --> 00:01:30.346
in the world.

00:01:30.346 --> 00:01:33.492
All the stars are
hand-painted one dot at a time

00:01:33.492 --> 00:01:36.659
with glow in the dark, luminous paint.

00:01:37.553 --> 00:01:40.072
It took about five months.

00:01:40.072 --> 00:01:43.020
This is the only planetarium
in the whole world

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:47.103
that has the night sky as
glow in the dark paint.

00:01:48.046 --> 00:01:49.994
This is beyond normal,

00:01:49.994 --> 00:01:53.927
but some of us actually
put our dream into reality

00:01:53.927 --> 00:01:54.760
and do it.

00:01:56.754 --> 00:01:58.794
I took ordinary materials,

00:01:58.794 --> 00:02:02.711
and I made something
extraordinary out of them.

